pokeheartgold-speed-spd4.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies the patches in name order): Walk, Surf and Run speed (spd4), part of the
port's per-part speed options (docs/speed-options.md "Platinum and HeartGold/SoulSilver"; the others are pokeheartgold-speed.patch's
Text speed and their own patch files). The player's step pick (sub_0205D4B4 in unk_0205CB48_0205D450_0205D4B4_0205D4B4.c: 0xc walk,
0x58 run, 0x10 Surf) swaps the walk action 0xc (8 frames a tile) for 0x10 (2x) or 0x14 (4x) and the Surf action 0x10 (4 frames) for
0x14 (2x and 4x: 0x54's 1-frame step stops Platinum's Surf legs), through PortSpeed4_WalkCode / PortSpeed4_SurfCode, which ask
port/game/speed_gen4.c (the WalkSpeed / SurfSpeed settings, Black's). The following Pokemon copies the action the pick gives
(ov01_02205990), but its follow code (one request per player step, one held; a wait frame in state 1 and one after each of its
steps) dropped requests when the player's step was 2 frames and the Pokemon then stayed tiles behind (route hg cherry at Walk 4x).
While a faster Walk or Run is set and a follower is active (the pick tells port/game/speed_gen4.c: PortSpeed4_SetFollower,
PortSpeed4_FollowFast) the follow code steps at once (sub_02065A4C's state 1, sub_02065C2C's step end) and a Pokemon whose step
ended away from the player's last tile steps again. Run speed: the run command (cmds 88-91, 4 px a frame for 4 frames, the run animation) is remade by
unk_02062108_020626AC.c's own Step0s (PortSpeed4_InitRun) for the player's object only: 8 px for 2 frames at 2x, 16 px for 1 at
4x; no new command rows (the follower and the checks that read the action code still see 0x58; the follower copies the run as the
walk 0x10, or at a faster Run speed as 0x14 or 0x54: unk_020658D4_02065D78_02065D78.c, unk_020658D4_02065DB4.c). A faster run step
keeps its run animation through its frames (map_object.c sub_0205F330), the 1-frame step's end is reported
(PlayerAvatar_UpdateMovement), and the map loader's tracker looks twice a frame at Run 4x so it sees each 1-frame step's start and
end (MapLoadManager_Tick; docs/speed-options.md). NPCs, scripts, the bike and jumps keep the game's. At every default setting each
hunk is exactly the game's own code path. The DS build never sees the patch.
